
  Step 5/17 • Each worktree's space

  ✓ What runs: postgres, redis, mailpit, admin, api, web, worker, migrate, seed
  ✓ Run once: migrate, seed
  ✓ Root dev script: one by one
  ✓ Shared: postgres, mailpit

  What each worktree gets of a shared service: service.name=its space ({worktree} filled in), service.create=
  and service.remove=the commands that make and drop it, its name in $WTM_NAMESPACE (repeatable; a service
  with no name gets nothing of its own)

›
  postgres.name=acme_{worktree}
  postgres.create=docker compose exec -T postgres createdb -U postgres "$WTM_NAMESPACE"
  postgres.remove=docker compose exec -T postgres dropdb -U postgres --if-exists "$WTM_NAMESPACE"

  tab add another • backspace remove last • enter confirm • esc back
